{"body":{"text":["A component is a holon, and says in it only what it says, its `input`, and its body where it is data. The code that realizes it on the web is the web's components' own, in `components/web/`, which give the web's chassis, in `chassis/web/`, the map of it, found by the component's id and never its name (`components/web/realized.ts`); components realized on another surface keep a map of their own. The chassis names no component: whoever starts it gives it the components, what each is called, and the ones it draws for its own cases, the one that chooses where several could draw a value, the fallback, and Problem, as OpenLight's chassis mounted components of its own (21/39); it stands apart from the components it draws, since a local chassis will come beside the web's: \"we know we're going to want local chassis anyway\" (20/19). *The chassis broken away, the author's, 20/17 and 20/19; where the code lies the session's (20/18); built.* Some components, as the reader and search, are defined wholly in the field, as layout and data (15/19). *Components as holons, settled 2026-11-11.* A component declares its `input` as a function does, a list of types matched by type (18/27), and is applied by a use, which names it and gives it what it is to show; mount folds into use, \"I'm fine with the dropping mount until we feel the need of it again\" (18/71). *Settled, 18/93; built. The chassis given a component for its own case of a problem, the author's, 21/39; built.*"]},"id":"1M86J2QWG2VF000","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A component is a function of what it is given and of the field, and keeps no state of the field: \"The UI was always supposed to be stateless\" (21/63). What the browser keeps for convenience stands apart, how a list was last shown and whether the bar is open; whether it belongs in the field is the path State in buffers. A component is given `io`, the chassis's actions where it is drawn, passed in rather than called on an object of its own, the author liking no objects with methods (21/39), and named after his word for what meets the outside, \"It's I/O\" (16/5): `read`, the field as it renders, the value, or nothing until it answers; `ask`, the field once, as a handler does; `draw`, a value within it, by whatever draws that; `propose`, a value back through the way back, committed; `remove`, it taken out of the list it stands in; and `pick`, where a component is to be chosen. \"We do need the consuming of the field in components to be simple\" (21/3); \"If I invoke a read, of course the chassis will be aware of me invoking a read. … And when it comes in, it's just a value. Why can't I use that value directly?\" (21/57). No helper stands between: \"I don't understand the point of live at all, of using a helper at all\" (21/55). *A component a plain function over values and stateless, the author's, 21/57 and 21/63; no helper his, 21/55; the actions the session's, he having asked for few (21/53, 21/54); `io` the session's offer, taken by the author (21/50, 21/51); built.*"]},"id":"1M86J2QWG2VF001","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A component reads by an expression of the language written in its code as a template, ``q`print(${step})` ``: \"let's use template literals for now\" (21/47). The language reads the template's text as a lambda over its holes, once for each template, and the chassis applies that lambda to what is put into them, each quoted, so a value is never read as words. Its functions are named by their bare names, which a function of the same name in any store mounted would make ambiguous; naming them by route was weighed, and left as the path Templates naming functions by route. A builder of uses in TypeScript, which the author asked to have explored (21/45), was taken as far as it goes, calls as uses and lambdas traced, JavaScript's own operators a silent trap (21/46), and set aside for now: the path A native builder for expressions. The author sees an IDE built on the field, open-ended and WYSIWYG, with AI working in it, as \"a great way to make big impact with this project\", and how \"we break away the harness\"; once there, \"everything's going to be different anyway\" (21/47). *Templates for now, the author's, 21/47; how they are read the session's; built.*"]},"id":"1M86J2QWG2VF002","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The chassis does for every component what each would else do for itself, the reads being, in the author's words, the \"state management\" of the \"framework\" (21/31). The expressions every component reads in one turn it asks as one read of the engine, kept live, each told its own part of the answer, and each asked alone again where that one read fails; a read asked whole, as Answer's, is asked alone. It renders a component again when what it is given changes, or an answer says something new, and lays the new render over the page, changing only what differs, so focus, a caret and a scroll stay (21/60); keeps each drawing in place by its key, a holon by its id, a drawing by the uses it was reached through, the field giving the keys the author held lists need (21/29); shows a drawing made anew, or a render waiting on its reads, once every read within it has answered, so nothing shows piece by piece, or after two seconds; and stands each drawing as a boundary, the component Problem drawn in its place, given what failed, where what it is given, a read it asks or its render fails: \"failure handling as error boundaries make sense and that the chassis then mount the error component\" (21/39). Where the way back finds no change, the chassis marks the place fixed, `data-fixed` on its host, which no render of that drawing undoes. It draws nothing of its own but a host for each drawing and a line where even Problem cannot draw; the inspector and the bar showing the page busy are the page's (21/34). A component for waiting, a skeleton, waits: \"a waiting component has to be unique for that component and that enters the whole dilemma of good DX\" (21/41), the path Skeletons while waiting; so do reads streamed as they come, which the author finds an interesting possibility \"as long as it shows it is still rendering\" (21/29). A component holding what the browser keeps for it, as the input does with what is typed and what completion offers, gives its node with how to update it, and is updated in place of rendering. *Problems as boundaries with a component of their own, the author's (21/39); batching as the framework's state his (21/31); keys for lists his (21/29); a render only where something changed on his ground, \"The UI should only update if it's actually a change that actually changes\" (21/57); the morph, waiting before showing and the mark fixed the session's (21/36, 21/60, 21/74), the last at his \"Don't ship broken things\" (21/73); built, 271 tests passing.*"]},"id":"1M86J2QWG2VF003","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A component's look is the chassis's too, and shipped with the components, not with the site: \"the components look probably should be shipped with them. That's the component's responsibility\" (19/15). Styling has its degree, the author said, while what looks wholly different may want other components; so the look's variables are opened, to be tuned, by a knob component perhaps, and later taken from the field (19/15). On the web it stands in `components/web/look/`, a stylesheet for each component with a look of its own, beneath them the page's ground and the tokens; one built stylesheet and the faces are what a site links, and beside it the chassis's own, in `chassis/web/look/`, and the inspector's, the page's, in `site/`; the bar showing the page busy keeps its look among the components'. The material, a stylesheet kept as text in glass that nothing read, was let go with its type: \"I don't see the point of the material\" (19/13, 19/15). *The look shipped with the components, its variables opened and the material let go, the author's, 19/15; its layout the session's; built.*"]},"id":"1M86J2QWG2VF004","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["What a use naming no component gives is drawn by the component that takes it, found by `taking`, a function of the language, not the chassis's: of the functions or components it is given to choose among, those that take all that is given, as a use giving it would be judged, some placeholder taking something given of a type of the field it takes. So a brief draws as a brief, and a list with the direction it runs as a list. Whether a function or a component takes what is given is the native `takes`, giving what each placeholder takes, or null: native because how a use's args meet an input is the evaluator's own, so the rule is written once and the chassis rebuilds nothing of the engine. The author asked for finding as one simple expression: \"It should just be one simple expression, right?\" (20/25), matching every argument: \"we match against multiple arguments, not only one\" (20/27). A component over a kind of value alone, a list or a string, is never found so, since many take one shape for different ends, and is drawn only where a use names it; what nothing takes by a type is drawn by the fallback the chassis is given, Value, showing any holon as its values, so nothing is left unshown, and what holds no holon is given it at once, nothing read. One found draws it and is found again each time, nothing written into the field as the chassis draws, which it did until the session found and let it go (21/26, 21/36); where several fit, a chooser lists them and the person's pick is drawn for the page, never guessed. How a component is to be chosen, as chrome given the chassis or in the context menu, the author has not settled: \"in this I'm sceptical of the chassis doing anything UI related\" (21/33); \"Not sure that is the right solution\", taking \"hardwired for now\" (21/35). *Open: the path Choosing a component as chrome.* *Finding as one expression over every argument, the author's (20/25, 20/27); takes and taking the session's (20/28); the name `taking` the session's, taken by the author (20/32, 20/33); built.*"]},"id":"1M86J2QWG2VF005","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Layout as data was held to the test of the search bar, which takes a query and shows its steps as pills: `steps` gives the query's steps, `each` makes one use of the pill per step, and a list lays them beside an input; removing a pill flows back through the way back of each, then `chain`, then `print`, into the address (18/72). The pill and the input are code at the leaves, the arrangement around them data. \"If it can't, then we have a problem with layout as data\" (18/71). Built, the test came out mixed: the arrangement is data, the reader laying search above the answer and search laying the text's steps as pills beside the input, both shipped in glass, while the leaves, pill, input, list and answer, the ways back through each, steps and chain, and dropping an item from a list when its × is pressed are code (18/98). *Proposed, 18/72; built.* Pills taken from the text itself, given plain text, were weighed and not taken, print's tidying kept at the author's doubt (21/66, 21/67): the path Pills from the text."]},"id":"1M86J2QWG2VF006","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Since components render on the chassis, a move takes about 70 to 210 ms in the browser, where it took 45 to 150: the path Moves slower than before. Timed step by step (21/84): the query committed, the root read again while the reads of the page before ran again, a component found by type in 20 to 33 ms (the path Finding by type on every move), then reads waiting on the reads before them, the 79 functions about 50 ms of it and a list's table a second round after its cards (the path The table's second round). Every kept read is worked out again, whole, whenever a store it stood on moves, and every read stands on every store; component renders are already only where something changed, the waste the engine's, as the session found (21/89). The author's view: only reads receiving a change should run again, \"not the whole page\" (21/77), \"only the changes should be broadcasted\" (21/83). A store telling, with its head, what its commits touched, and a kept read running again only where it read one, was built and reverted for losing changes silently (21/93), under the author's rule: \"It is important the engine does not get convoluted and no debt is made. Solutions must be pristine and simple and thought through under the principles and values of the system\" (21/86). *That rule settled, 21/86.* A kept read checking again, by content, the holons it used was weighed and held by the session, its gain too small for a second path in the engine (21/95), against his condition, \"if it is simple and provides strong benefit it makes sense\" (21/94): the path A kept read checking what it used. Re-deriving only where a change flows is, the author says, \"for the future … probably a requirement of an engine\" (21/90), the bigger step its successor (21/96). *Leaning, 21/90; open, the thread Reads re-derived where a change flows.* The engine keeps no state so that stores may become fast enough to stand apart: \"the stores themselves could be effective enough to be external, but that is a very long time\" (21/75)."]},"id":"1M86J2QWG2VF007","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The author's review of the components and the chassis,** which the next session takes (21/98), the components now plain functions of what they are given and the field, read through `io` (21/51, 21/72)."]},"id":"1M86J2QWG2VF008","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The old wiki's fate:** whether The wiki, kept as it stood, is let go, as the author leaned to if Knowledge holds all it does (18/105), and whether the reasoning it alone holds comes into Knowledge first. *Open, awaiting the author.*"]},"id":"1M86J2QWG2VF009","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Fewer passes to the stores:** \"I would thikn it shouldn t need many passes to the store if we have the right native vocabulary\" (19/72). A brief is now read in one read, and what a read applies learned a layer at a time, each function it names asked whole (20/16, 20/34); it is still learned every read, and knowing it across reads would be the engine keeping something, a deeper discussion the author set apart: \"architecturally, that's not what we drew\" (20/11). The reads of a page run again on each move of the query, where the author holds only reads receiving a change should (21/77); re-deriving only where a change flows is, he says, \"for the future … probably a requirement of an engine\" (21/90), the successor (21/96). *Open; the thread Reads re-derived where a change flows.*"]},"id":"1M86J2QWG2VF00A","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
