{"body":{"text":["The query is a buffer, holding only the present, kept as one with the address, `?q=`: loading, back and forward type the address into it, each change replaces the address, and pressing Enter or following a link pushes a step, so a link moves within the page and the engine keeps running. What is typed goes back, on Enter, from where the input is drawn to the buffer's text, which alone is written; as one types, only completion is offered. The page names its stores in its own code, as the author leaned: \"the site that we want built will define its stores in the sites. ts i would think\" (11/7), and took at 18/17: \"on point three: ok\". *Settled, 18/17.*"]},"id":"1M86J2QWG2VF00K","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}